  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Region Media Strengthening Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will address challenges to public interest media at audience, practitioner, organisational and system levels in 6 Pacific Island Countries (PICs) leading to a healthier information ecosystem, where a steady flow of trusted and engaging public interest media content reaches and engages audiences and builds resilience to mis-and disinformation, with magnified sectoral support for and defence of the space for public interest media and media freedom. Proposed countries of implementation include Fiji, Solomon Islands, Papua New Guinea, Samoa, Tonga, and Vanuatu.</narrative>
  </description>
